(SAMPLE MARINE SM-30 MARINE DIESEL - OWNER'S MANUAL   \(fictional - sample data\)) Tj
T* (Section 6: Periodic maintenance \(excerpt, pages 41-42\)) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (6.1 General) Tj
T* (Do maintenance at the engine-hour interval or the calendar interval,) Tj
T* (whichever comes first. An engine used little still needs its yearly) Tj
T* (service, because oil and coolant age even when the engine does not run.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (6.2 Maintenance schedule) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (ITEM                                 HOURS      CALENDAR) Tj
T* (Engine oil and oil filter            100 h      12 months) Tj
T* (Fuel filter element                  200 h      12 months) Tj
T* (Raw-water pump impeller              250 h      24 months) Tj
T* (Coolant \(replace\)                    1,000 h    24 months) Tj
T* (Valve clearance \(check and adjust\)   500 h      -) Tj
T* (Drive belt \(inspect / replace\)       250 h      24 months) Tj
T* (Zinc anodes in heat exchanger        100 h      6 months) Tj
T* (Air intake filter \(clean\)            100 h      12 months) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (6.3 Engine oil) Tj
T* (Capacity with filter: 4.8 quarts \(4.5 liters\).) Tj
T* (Use oil rated API CH-4 or better, SAE 15W-40 above 5 C.) Tj
T* (Check the level every day of use, with the engine stopped and level.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (6.4 Raw-water impeller) Tj
T* (Close the seacock before opening the pump cover. Replace the impeller if) Tj
T* (any vane is cracked, set or missing, and always carry a spare on board.) Tj
T* (Running the pump dry for more than 30 seconds damages the impeller.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (6.5 Winter lay-up) Tj
T* (Change the oil before lay-up, not after, so acidic used oil does not sit) Tj
T* (in the engine. Flush the raw-water circuit with non-toxic antifreeze.) Tj
ET
